1
00:00:10,051 --> 00:00:11,219
<i>Grandma, thanks to you,</i>

2
00:00:11,302 --> 00:00:14,889
I may be falling in love
for the first time!

3
00:00:15,849 --> 00:00:20,562
He doesn't need to put on a show.
I prefer him as he is.

4
00:00:20,645 --> 00:00:23,022
You like him as he is?

5
00:00:23,106 --> 00:00:26,776
-Yay!
-Konta! Congratulations!

6
00:00:28,153 --> 00:00:30,113
-You did it!
-Thanks, Rinrin.

7
00:00:30,196 --> 00:00:31,406
Summer festival?

8
00:00:31,990 --> 00:00:33,241
Shall I guide you?

9
00:00:33,324 --> 00:00:35,035
Well, I'll go take a quick look.

10
00:00:35,118 --> 00:00:37,495
Hey, the two of them left together.

11
00:00:38,079 --> 00:00:40,999
<i>The fates of Grim Reapers</i>
<i>and humans do not cross.</i>

12
00:00:42,083 --> 00:00:45,962
<i>With death, their lives are fulfilled.</i>

13
00:01:01,728 --> 00:01:02,979
Mr. Nishigami.

14
00:01:11,863 --> 00:01:14,032
Another hot day, huh?

15
00:01:15,909 --> 00:01:17,202
Yes.

16
00:01:28,046 --> 00:01:29,255
I see.

17
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:30,840
Orange peels…

18
00:01:30,924 --> 00:01:32,759
How do you make them?

19
00:01:32,842 --> 00:01:34,761
They're surprisingly easy to make.

20
00:01:35,512 --> 00:01:37,430
If you want, we can make them together.

21
00:01:37,514 --> 00:01:38,890
No, I can't do it.

22
00:01:38,973 --> 00:01:40,266
You can!

23
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:41,309
Here!

24
00:01:41,935 --> 00:01:42,811
Here we go.

25
00:01:44,646 --> 00:01:46,815
What do I do with this?

26
00:01:46,898 --> 00:01:48,066
Huh? Oh, right.

27
00:01:49,567 --> 00:01:50,860
Put it on…

28
00:01:51,736 --> 00:01:52,570
There.

29
00:01:56,407 --> 00:01:58,827
Then, tie this in the front.

30
00:01:58,910 --> 00:02:00,036
All right.

31
00:02:02,330 --> 00:02:04,332
You two, your ice cream is going to melt.

32
00:02:05,041 --> 00:02:05,875
What?

33
00:02:07,752 --> 00:02:11,422
-Something's up…
-Maybe we shouldn't be here?

34
00:02:13,716 --> 00:02:15,677
Yo, Mr. Nishigami!

35
00:02:15,760 --> 00:02:17,428
That apron looks good on you.

36
00:02:18,054 --> 00:02:19,347
-Oh, Midori!
-Yes?

37
00:02:19,430 --> 00:02:21,182
Should I get some more beer?

38
00:02:21,266 --> 00:02:23,560
-Oh, please do. Thanks.
-Okay.

39
00:02:23,643 --> 00:02:26,187
Wait, Konta. I'm going with you. May I?

40
00:02:26,271 --> 00:02:27,272
Wait, really?

41
00:02:27,355 --> 00:02:29,607
Oh, that's a big help. Let's go then!

42
00:02:29,691 --> 00:02:31,651
Yeah, let's go together.

43
00:02:32,652 --> 00:02:36,030
Oh, no. I'm the only one
without any summer romance!

44
00:02:39,075 --> 00:02:40,034
Tetsuro!

45
00:02:40,118 --> 00:02:41,035
Yes?

46
00:02:41,578 --> 00:02:42,829
Going fishing?

47
00:02:42,912 --> 00:02:44,914
I'm going to fish for horse mackerel.

48
00:02:45,498 --> 00:02:46,833
Shall I come along with you?

49
00:02:47,917 --> 00:02:49,043
Sure.

50
00:02:49,127 --> 00:02:50,378
Let's hurry!

51
00:03:25,371 --> 00:03:26,956
-Butterfly.
-Butterfly!

52
00:03:27,457 --> 00:03:29,334
Hey, Konta, how did it go?

53
00:03:29,417 --> 00:03:31,586
The movie. <i>The Great Tenpo Famine</i>?

54
00:03:31,669 --> 00:03:33,671
Oh, they sent over the script.

55
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:37,592
What are you grinning for?

56
00:03:37,675 --> 00:03:40,178
Well, you see, I actually have lines.

57
00:03:40,261 --> 00:03:42,305
Seriously? That's amazing, Konta!

58
00:03:42,388 --> 00:03:44,224
Well, it's only one line, though.

59
00:03:46,517 --> 00:03:50,730
In order to survive,
you even have to eat grass!

60
00:03:51,439 --> 00:03:53,983
Wow, getting lines is amazing!

61
00:03:54,817 --> 00:03:56,903
It's all thanks to the documentary.

62
00:03:59,113 --> 00:04:01,074
All right, let's race to the sea.

63
00:04:01,157 --> 00:04:02,158
Ready, go!

64
00:04:02,242 --> 00:04:03,326
Hey, wait!

65
00:04:03,409 --> 00:04:04,953
I won't lose, okay?

66
00:04:06,037 --> 00:04:07,830
I'm not going to lose!

67
00:04:07,914 --> 00:04:08,873
Hey!

68
00:04:20,510 --> 00:04:23,346
Mr. Nishigami,
you are surprisingly clumsy.

69
00:04:23,972 --> 00:04:25,014
I'm sorry.

70
00:04:26,391 --> 00:04:29,769
I am not very used to this.

71
00:04:29,852 --> 00:04:31,020
It's okay.

72
00:04:31,104 --> 00:04:32,397
Just take it slow.

73
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:34,274
Oh, watch your hands.

74
00:04:34,357 --> 00:04:35,566
Okay.

75
00:04:40,363 --> 00:04:41,489
What?

76
00:04:42,907 --> 00:04:44,075
This…

77
00:04:44,158 --> 00:04:45,702
is too thick!

78
00:04:45,785 --> 00:04:47,370
This is a wedge cut.

79
00:04:47,453 --> 00:04:48,746
It's hard to eat.

80
00:04:50,915 --> 00:04:53,751
-I'm sorry. Then, I'll…
-Yes?

81
00:04:54,752 --> 00:04:55,920
What?

82
00:05:01,676 --> 00:05:02,719
So bitter.

83
00:05:18,443 --> 00:05:20,820
I've never done this before.

84
00:05:21,362 --> 00:05:22,780
Fishing is nice, huh.

85
00:05:24,198 --> 00:05:27,994
Just staring blankly at the sea
without thinking about anything.

86
00:05:28,077 --> 00:05:29,662
What a luxury.

87
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:31,581
Yes.

88
00:05:32,623 --> 00:05:36,627
After coming here,
I've discovered how fun fishing is.

89
00:05:37,628 --> 00:05:41,883
I mean, it's certainly better than SNS.

90
00:05:43,718 --> 00:05:45,928
Oh, you mean social media.

91
00:05:46,012 --> 00:05:47,472
I don't use any.

92
00:05:49,640 --> 00:05:52,602
You know, my ex,

93
00:05:53,352 --> 00:05:56,564
he checks my social media quite a bit,

94
00:05:57,565 --> 00:05:59,525
and he leaves likes often.

95
00:06:00,902 --> 00:06:02,487
Oh, here it comes!

96
00:06:02,570 --> 00:06:06,657
-Here it comes!
-You got something! All right!

97
00:06:07,366 --> 00:06:09,035
Oh, wow!

98
00:06:09,118 --> 00:06:10,328
Wow!

99
00:06:10,411 --> 00:06:13,372
You got the first fish!

100
00:06:13,456 --> 00:06:14,582
Nice.

101
00:06:16,542 --> 00:06:18,336
And… posted.

102
00:06:18,419 --> 00:06:19,670
You're posting it?

103
00:06:20,713 --> 00:06:22,256
Oh! I did it without thinking!

104
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:24,092
Yikes, I'm addicted.

105
00:06:24,175 --> 00:06:27,095
But I'm glad it wasn't a total bust.

106
00:06:27,178 --> 00:06:28,596
Midori will be happy.

107
00:06:29,305 --> 00:06:31,224
What? Bust?

108
00:06:31,307 --> 00:06:33,017
It's a fishing term.

109
00:06:33,101 --> 00:06:35,895
If you don't catch a single fish,
it's called a bust.

110
00:06:38,314 --> 00:06:39,690
But why Midori?

111
00:06:39,774 --> 00:06:41,984
Oh, nothing.

112
00:06:42,068 --> 00:06:47,907
It's just that Midori likes cooking,
so I thought she would be happy.

113
00:06:47,990 --> 00:06:49,408
I see.

114
00:06:51,911 --> 00:06:53,204
All right.

115
00:06:53,287 --> 00:06:56,874
Let's catch a bunch
and have Midori make sashimi out of them.

116
00:06:56,958 --> 00:06:59,085
Let's buy some sake on the way back.

117
00:07:00,503 --> 00:07:03,047
-A sashimi party.
-Yeah!

118
00:07:03,131 --> 00:07:04,715
Party!

119
00:07:11,764 --> 00:07:13,766
Mr. Nishigami…

120
00:07:15,810 --> 00:07:18,146
Do you have a girlfriend?

121
00:07:20,148 --> 00:07:21,274
A girlfriend?

122
00:07:23,901 --> 00:07:25,027
No.

123
00:07:25,111 --> 00:07:28,114
I have no one like that.

124
00:07:30,324 --> 00:07:31,576
I see.

125
00:07:33,119 --> 00:07:36,456
Oh, by the way, I've never had one either.

126
00:07:36,539 --> 00:07:37,582
Surprising, right?

127
00:07:37,665 --> 00:07:39,459
I'm already 28.

128
00:07:39,542 --> 00:07:41,043
It's a red flag, isn't it?

129
00:07:42,086 --> 00:07:43,337
Is that so?

130
00:08:06,068 --> 00:08:07,487
Heave-ho.

131
00:08:08,112 --> 00:08:10,114
It's so windy today.

132
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:11,908
Hup.

133
00:08:11,991 --> 00:08:13,784
-Rinrin!
-Yes?

134
00:08:14,368 --> 00:08:15,995
-What?
-I bought juice.

135
00:08:16,078 --> 00:08:17,955
-Huh? What kind of juice?
-Take a guess!

136
00:08:18,039 --> 00:08:19,665
What could it be? Coffee…

137
00:08:19,749 --> 00:08:21,083
-Coke.
-Oh, it's Coke.

138
00:08:21,167 --> 00:08:23,920
-You only got the "co" right.
-I did. Thank you.

139
00:08:24,003 --> 00:08:25,588
You were shaking it, right?

140
00:08:25,671 --> 00:08:27,548
-Did I? It will be fine.
-Will it?

141
00:08:28,341 --> 00:08:31,219
-No! What terrible luck!
-No!

142
00:08:31,302 --> 00:08:33,471
-It's all over me!
-Sorry, Rinrin!

143
00:08:39,894 --> 00:08:40,978
Hey, so…

144
00:08:41,729 --> 00:08:42,772
What?

145
00:08:44,732 --> 00:08:46,108
What exactly

146
00:08:47,818 --> 00:08:50,363
is our relationship right now?

147
00:08:52,406 --> 00:08:54,116
What kind of relationship…

148
00:08:55,243 --> 00:08:57,453
Well, about that…

149
00:08:58,079 --> 00:09:01,791
The other day, you know, during <i>Obon</i>,

150
00:09:02,708 --> 00:09:04,544
we, you know…

151
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:08,965
Do you…

152
00:09:10,633 --> 00:09:12,593
think we can be a couple?

153
00:09:20,851 --> 00:09:26,232
"A woman's heart
is a deep ocean of secrets."

154
00:09:26,315 --> 00:09:27,441
Hey!

155
00:09:27,525 --> 00:09:30,319
Is that Rose's famous line from <i>Titanic</i>?

156
00:09:30,403 --> 00:09:33,072
Truly an actor!
You remembered it from just a line.

157
00:09:33,155 --> 00:09:36,033
No, I love <i>Titanic</i>!
I remember lots of lines from it.

158
00:09:36,117 --> 00:09:37,827
So you watched the dubbed version?

159
00:09:37,910 --> 00:09:39,579
Well, of course. I don't know English.

160
00:09:42,790 --> 00:09:45,167
Between Rose and Jack,

161
00:09:45,251 --> 00:09:48,004
do you think the concept
of "dating" even existed?

162
00:09:48,087 --> 00:09:49,797
I don't know.

163
00:09:50,423 --> 00:09:52,133
They fell in love instantly,

164
00:09:52,216 --> 00:09:55,511
and before they could think about dating,
the ship went bam!

165
00:09:56,470 --> 00:10:02,560
Well, let's do fun things together,
then I'll think about us dating.

166
00:10:03,144 --> 00:10:04,937
Wait, so…

167
00:10:05,021 --> 00:10:06,647
I have a chance?

168
00:10:09,859 --> 00:10:12,486
All right, let's practice acting.

169
00:10:12,570 --> 00:10:13,613
-What?
-Oh!

170
00:10:13,696 --> 00:10:16,616
I want to play <i>Titanic </i>on that boat.

171
00:10:16,699 --> 00:10:18,117
Huh, on that fishing boat?

172
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:19,744
-Yeah!
-Sure.

173
00:10:19,827 --> 00:10:21,537
-Really?
-Wait, Rinrin, your bag!

174
00:10:24,290 --> 00:10:28,044
-The sea is so vast and blue.
-Vast and blue!

175
00:10:28,878 --> 00:10:30,171
Konta!

176
00:10:30,254 --> 00:10:31,255
What, Rinrin?

177
00:10:31,339 --> 00:10:37,511
When you become famous and rich,
can you make me your stay-at-home wife?

178
00:10:37,595 --> 00:10:38,721
What?

179
00:10:39,513 --> 00:10:42,141
Is this a proposal?

180
00:10:42,224 --> 00:10:48,022
If you become a popular actor,
I won't have to work anymore, right?

181
00:10:48,105 --> 00:10:51,776
I can just relax here
like this forever, right?

182
00:10:53,778 --> 00:10:55,071
All right.

183
00:10:55,154 --> 00:10:56,989
-Rinrin, here.
-Oh, okay.

184
00:10:57,073 --> 00:10:58,074
There you go.

185
00:11:03,037 --> 00:11:05,039
I will do my best!

186
00:11:06,582 --> 00:11:08,042
For you, Rinrin!

187
00:11:08,125 --> 00:11:10,628
I'll be the biggest star!

188
00:11:11,295 --> 00:11:12,671
Good luck!

189
00:11:13,297 --> 00:11:14,632
Rinrin!

190
00:11:14,715 --> 00:11:15,716
What?

191
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:17,968
Can I say something
I like about you, Rinrin?

192
00:11:18,052 --> 00:11:19,136
Sure!

193
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:20,763
Rinrin,

194
00:11:22,431 --> 00:11:23,891
your skin is so fair!

195
00:11:24,975 --> 00:11:26,477
What are those two doing?

196
00:11:33,275 --> 00:11:34,610
For some reason,

197
00:11:34,693 --> 00:11:39,156
when people stand in front of the sea,
they can't help but reenact <i>Titanic</i>.

198
00:11:40,324 --> 00:11:41,617
Huh? Who are you?

199
00:11:42,243 --> 00:11:43,494
How is it?

200
00:11:43,577 --> 00:11:45,621
Enjoying the life you have left?

201
00:11:45,704 --> 00:11:47,415
It's nice to be young.

202
00:11:47,498 --> 00:11:49,166
The life we have left?

203
00:11:49,250 --> 00:11:51,127
Yes, we're having fun…

204
00:11:51,210 --> 00:11:52,044
fishing.

205
00:11:52,586 --> 00:11:53,504
Oh, I see.

206
00:11:53,587 --> 00:11:55,423
Okay. That's a good thing.

207
00:11:55,506 --> 00:11:56,465
It's good.

208
00:11:56,549 --> 00:11:57,758
-Huh?
-It's good.

209
00:11:59,093 --> 00:12:00,845
It's nice to be young…

210
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:12,148
Do you think she and Konta are dating?

211
00:12:12,231 --> 00:12:15,651
They kissed. It doesn't
necessarily mean they're dating.

212
00:12:15,734 --> 00:12:16,569
What?

213
00:12:17,111 --> 00:12:19,405
What do you mean by that?

214
00:12:21,740 --> 00:12:24,785
By the way,
you're interested in Midori, aren't you?

215
00:12:28,038 --> 00:12:29,081
What?

216
00:12:29,165 --> 00:12:30,916
Huh, wait?

217
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:32,209
Am I?

218
00:12:33,294 --> 00:12:34,712
You don't even know?

219
00:12:35,504 --> 00:12:36,755
You like her, for sure.

220
00:12:36,839 --> 00:12:40,468
Look, you're even fishing for her sake.

221
00:12:41,886 --> 00:12:43,554
Midori is a good girl.

222
00:12:43,637 --> 00:12:45,890
She's a hard worker, and she's cute.

223
00:12:48,100 --> 00:12:49,977
I like her too.

224
00:12:50,895 --> 00:12:52,980
But she probably…

225
00:13:02,656 --> 00:13:04,617
Sun-drying is nice, isn't it?

226
00:13:05,117 --> 00:13:08,996
They absorb a lot of sunlight,
so I'm sure they will turn out delicious.

227
00:13:09,788 --> 00:13:11,290
By drying them out like this,

228
00:13:12,374 --> 00:13:14,001
what will you achieve, in the end?

229
00:13:14,877 --> 00:13:17,838
I don't really understand it.

230
00:13:24,053 --> 00:13:25,804
I'm home!

231
00:13:25,888 --> 00:13:26,764
Welcome home.

232
00:13:27,348 --> 00:13:29,099
-Midori, look.
-What is it?

233
00:13:29,183 --> 00:13:30,518
-Midori.
-Hm?

234
00:13:30,601 --> 00:13:32,019
-We got a huge catch!
-What?

235
00:13:33,479 --> 00:13:34,939
Oh, wow!

236
00:13:35,022 --> 00:13:36,357
Now work your magic, Chef.

237
00:13:36,440 --> 00:13:38,150
I'm raring to go.

238
00:13:38,234 --> 00:13:39,193
I'll help too.

239
00:13:39,276 --> 00:13:41,153
-Okay.
-We've got to make sashimi.

240
00:13:41,237 --> 00:13:43,113
-Yeah!
-Sashimi!

241
00:13:43,197 --> 00:13:49,495
<i>Sashimi!</i>

242
00:13:49,578 --> 00:13:51,789
-What about fried?
-Sounds good too!

243
00:13:51,872 --> 00:13:54,583
<i>Fried!</i>

244
00:13:55,125 --> 00:13:56,252
Make <i>nanbanzuke</i>!

245
00:13:56,752 --> 00:13:59,421
<i>Nanbanzuke!</i>

246
00:14:00,339 --> 00:14:03,842
Tetsuro, bring out the plates.
Also, please chill the alcohol.

247
00:14:03,926 --> 00:14:04,969
Got it.

248
00:14:05,719 --> 00:14:07,638
As for you, Mr. Nishigami,

249
00:14:08,722 --> 00:14:12,810
can you cut some cucumber
to garnish the sashimi?

250
00:14:12,893 --> 00:14:15,145
-Here.
-Understood.

251
00:14:15,771 --> 00:14:18,816
Don't cut it too thick like earlier, okay?

252
00:14:19,608 --> 00:14:20,526
Yes.

253
00:14:21,402 --> 00:14:22,570
But…

254
00:14:22,653 --> 00:14:26,699
Cucumbers, even when thick,
are delicious, right?

255
00:14:26,782 --> 00:14:28,659
Well, true.

256
00:14:31,579 --> 00:14:34,456
-Look at this.
-What a nice photo!

257
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:37,126
-Oh, I'm so embarrassed! My dimples!
-They're cute!

258
00:14:37,209 --> 00:14:39,753
-Dimples are so cute!
-I have one too.

259
00:14:39,837 --> 00:14:41,505
No, you don't.

260
00:14:41,589 --> 00:14:45,551
Somehow, this vacation
is making everyone lovey-dovey.

261
00:14:52,391 --> 00:14:56,020
Now then, put your hands together.

262
00:14:56,103 --> 00:14:57,605
Put your hands together.

263
00:14:58,397 --> 00:14:59,356
Let's eat.

264
00:14:59,440 --> 00:15:01,442
Let's eat!

265
00:15:01,525 --> 00:15:03,527
-Tsumugi, pass the soy sauce.
-Okay.

266
00:15:03,611 --> 00:15:05,154
Tetsuro, shall I take this for you?

267
00:15:05,237 --> 00:15:07,197
-Thank you.
-Mr. Nishigami, here is the wasabi.

268
00:15:07,281 --> 00:15:09,742
-It looks good.
-Thank you.

269
00:15:09,825 --> 00:15:12,870
-All right, let's eat.
-Yum!

270
00:15:12,953 --> 00:15:15,998
When I remember that I caught these,
they taste twice as good.

271
00:15:16,707 --> 00:15:19,293
-Tsumugi caught two mackerels by herself.
-Really?

272
00:15:19,376 --> 00:15:22,004
-I might have a knack for fishing.
-Sure.

273
00:15:22,087 --> 00:15:26,300
By the way, Rinrin, Konta,
you two were reenacting <i>Titanic</i>, right?

274
00:15:26,383 --> 00:15:28,802
You were watching? How embarrassing.

275
00:15:28,886 --> 00:15:30,054
It's not embarrassing.

276
00:15:30,137 --> 00:15:32,973
In that moment,
we were totally Rose and Jack.

277
00:15:33,766 --> 00:15:35,017
What were you doing, Midori?

278
00:15:35,100 --> 00:15:38,687
I was making summer orange peels
with Mr. Nishigami, right?

279
00:15:39,605 --> 00:15:40,773
I had fun.

280
00:15:41,357 --> 00:15:42,399
Me too.

281
00:15:44,944 --> 00:15:45,819
So good.

282
00:15:46,570 --> 00:15:47,404
Here.

283
00:15:50,157 --> 00:15:51,283
It's so nice.

284
00:15:51,367 --> 00:15:52,868
There's salad too.

285
00:15:52,952 --> 00:15:55,579
-Thank you.
-Here you go, the usual salad.

286
00:15:55,663 --> 00:15:57,623
Thanks for the salad.

287
00:15:59,124 --> 00:16:01,043
-Here you go.
-Thanks.

288
00:16:02,002 --> 00:16:03,837
Be careful on your way home.

289
00:16:03,921 --> 00:16:05,172
See you tomorrow.

290
00:16:06,465 --> 00:16:08,342
Yeah. See you tomorrow.

291
00:16:24,358 --> 00:16:25,359
AI.

292
00:16:25,442 --> 00:16:26,610
This is Tetsuro.

293
00:16:28,153 --> 00:16:31,615
Right now, I'm on vacation.

294
00:16:32,533 --> 00:16:35,160
And when I see a woman
I'm spending time with

295
00:16:36,078 --> 00:16:39,123
looking happy with another person,

296
00:16:40,416 --> 00:16:42,292
another man…

297
00:16:44,378 --> 00:16:46,714
my chest tightens.

298
00:16:48,924 --> 00:16:51,427
And before I know it, I…

299
00:16:52,094 --> 00:16:54,596
I find myself thinking only about her.

300
00:16:56,473 --> 00:16:59,351
What is this feeling?

301
00:17:00,936 --> 00:17:02,229
<i>Tetsuro.</i>

302
00:17:03,480 --> 00:17:07,568
<i>That feeling of yours is most likely love.</i>

303
00:17:08,235 --> 00:17:09,278
Love?

304
00:17:10,070 --> 00:17:12,823
<i>By the way, you mentioned</i>
<i>you are on vacation.</i>

305
00:17:12,906 --> 00:17:16,118
<i>When humans are placed</i>
<i>in an unusual environment,</i>

306
00:17:16,201 --> 00:17:19,038
<i>they develop romantic feelings</i>
<i>more easily.</i>

307
00:17:20,289 --> 00:17:24,334
<i>Since AIs do not have emotions,</i>
<i>we cannot experience love or jealousy.</i>

308
00:17:24,418 --> 00:17:26,211
<i>We don't have vacations either.</i>

309
00:17:26,295 --> 00:17:28,589
<i>Vacations are a human privilege.</i>

310
00:17:29,798 --> 00:17:31,425
A human privilege?

311
00:17:32,301 --> 00:17:36,513
On vacation, people fall in love.
It's like a principle.

312
00:17:39,933 --> 00:17:41,268
A vacation

313
00:17:42,478 --> 00:17:43,604
principle?

314
00:17:52,154 --> 00:17:53,405
<i>Grim Reaper.</i>

315
00:17:54,198 --> 00:17:57,785
<i>Your recent actions</i>
<i>have been unacceptable.</i>

316
00:17:57,868 --> 00:18:00,120
<i>Do you understand what I mean?</i>

317
00:18:02,790 --> 00:18:03,957
I'm not sure.

318
00:18:04,708 --> 00:18:05,959
<i>Back during </i>Obon<i>,</i>

319
00:18:06,043 --> 00:18:09,505
<i>I was relieved that you understood</i>
<i>your position as a Grim Reaper,</i>

320
00:18:09,588 --> 00:18:13,175
<i>but now you're getting</i>
<i>friendly again with those people.</i>

321
00:18:14,009 --> 00:18:16,178
<i>The Sea God reported to me as much.</i>

322
00:18:16,261 --> 00:18:17,805
<i>What's wrong, Grim Reaper?</i>

323
00:18:17,888 --> 00:18:19,056
<i>Surely…</i>

324
00:18:19,139 --> 00:18:22,059
<i>You haven't forgotten</i>
<i>your mission, have you?</i>

325
00:18:27,231 --> 00:18:30,442
There is no way I would do such a thing.

326
00:18:30,526 --> 00:18:32,903
<i>Then why are you being their friend?</i>

327
00:18:37,491 --> 00:18:39,701
<i>As a Grim Reaper,</i>

328
00:18:39,785 --> 00:18:42,830
<i>there is no need for you</i>
<i>to have bonds with humans.</i>

329
00:18:42,913 --> 00:18:45,040
<i>Furthermore, given your position,</i>

330
00:18:45,124 --> 00:18:48,460
<i>falling in love with a human</i>
<i>is out of the question.</i>

331
00:18:48,544 --> 00:18:49,920
<i>Do you understand?</i>

332
00:18:52,256 --> 00:18:53,757
I do.

333
00:18:54,925 --> 00:18:56,635
<i>A typhoon is coming soon.</i>

334
00:18:57,344 --> 00:19:01,390
<i>Because of it, a landslide will occur,</i>
<i>and that villa will be destroyed.</i>

335
00:19:02,015 --> 00:19:05,894
<i>Those five you are</i>
<i>so close with will all die.</i>

336
00:19:07,020 --> 00:19:11,567
<i>Witnessing their demise</i>
<i>is your duty as a Grim Reaper.</i>

337
00:19:12,317 --> 00:19:14,319
<i>Don't forget that.</i>

338
00:19:17,698 --> 00:19:19,449
Be careful on your way home.

339
00:19:19,533 --> 00:19:20,492
See you tomorrow.

340
00:19:46,435 --> 00:19:48,145
<i>It's finally here.</i>

341
00:19:48,228 --> 00:19:50,189
<i>Midori's first love.</i>

342
00:19:50,272 --> 00:19:52,608
Hey, Midori, seriously?

343
00:19:52,691 --> 00:19:55,319
<i>Mr. Nishigami hasn't come</i>
<i>for the past two days.</i>

344
00:19:55,402 --> 00:19:57,362
He isn't playing
with Midori's feelings, right?

345
00:19:57,446 --> 00:19:58,488
Mr. Nishigami…

346
00:19:58,572 --> 00:20:00,824
You said, "See you tomorrow"…

347
00:20:00,908 --> 00:20:05,162
Because of this vacation,
it's now easier for us to fall in love.

348
00:20:05,245 --> 00:20:06,997
Why not make a move on Midori?

349
00:20:07,080 --> 00:20:08,165
<i>I…</i>

350
00:20:08,248 --> 00:20:09,625
Mr. Nishigami…

351
00:20:10,250 --> 00:20:11,543
<i>I'm the one at fault here.</i>

352
00:20:11,627 --> 00:20:12,711
Seriously?

353
00:20:12,794 --> 00:20:14,004
What is that supposed to mean?

354
00:20:14,087 --> 00:20:15,839
So it was all my misunderstanding?

355
00:20:16,506 --> 00:20:18,383
<i>Mr. Nishigami, could it be…</i>

356
00:20:19,051 --> 00:20:20,677
<i>you have come to dislike us?</i>

357
00:20:21,511 --> 00:20:22,471
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
